      #results thead th { white-space: normal; letter-spacing: 0; font-size: .68rem; }
      #results thead th:nth-child(1) { width: 3.25rem; }
      #results thead th:nth-child(2) { width: 34%; }
      #results thead th:nth-child(3) { width: 20%; }
      #results tbody th { overflow-wrap: break-word; }
      #results .col-video a { white-space: nowrap; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 400px) {
      #results .results-block { padding: 1rem .6rem; }
      #results th, #results td { padding: .5rem .3rem; }
      #results thead th:nth-child(1) { width: 2.5rem; }
      #results thead th:nth-child(2) { width: 36%; }
      #results thead th:nth-child(3) { width: 19%; }
    }
  </style>
{% endraw %}{% endblock %}

{% block main %}{% raw %}
<main id="main-content">
<section id="home" class="subhero">
  <div class="subhero-content">
    <div class="hero-wordmark hero-wordmark-sm" role="img" aria-label="EBiM Benchmark">
      <span class="hero-wordmark-mark">EBiM</span><span class="hero-wordmark-sub">Benchmark</span>
    </div>
    <div class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="index.html">Home</a>
      <span class="breadcrumb-sep">/</span>
      <a href="competition.html">Competition</a>
      <span class="breadcrumb-sep">/</span>
      <span class="breadcrumb-current">Final Results</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="subhero-title">Final Results</h1>
    <p class="subhero-subtitle">EBiM Benchmark Competition 2026</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="results">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="results-shell fade-in">

      <div class="results-intro">
        <p>These are the final rankings of the EBiM Benchmark Competition 2026. The organizers evaluated each team's Phase II policy on the physical Franka Mobile FR3 Duo at two of the three testbeds (Hamburg, Munich, Shanghai). Each task is ranked independently.</p>
        <p>Congratulations to the prize-winning teams. Thank you to every team that took part, and to the testbed teams in Hamburg, Munich, and Shanghai.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="results-block" id="task-1">
        <h2>Task 1 · Cable Routing &amp; Plugging</h2>
        <p>No prize is awarded for Task 1: the only Phase II submission could not be run on the real robot.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="results-block results-table-wrap" id="task-2">
        <table>
          <caption><h2>Task 2 · Deformable Material Handling</h2></caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Rank</th><th scope="col">Team</th><th scope="col">Award</th><th scope="col">Evaluation video</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="is-prize"><td class="col-rank">1</td><th scope="row">Hajimi</th><td>1st place</td><td class="col-video"><a href="https://cloud.uni-hamburg.de/s/KbgEojL2QQTgA4R?dir=/Hajimi" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Watch Hajimi's Task 2 evaluation videos">Watch</a></td></tr>
            <tr class="is-prize"><td class="col-rank">2</td><th scope="row">HKUST-RockAI</th><td>2nd place</td><td class="col-video"><a href="https://cloud.uni-hamburg.de/s/KbgEojL2QQTgA4R?dir=/HKUST-RockAI" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Watch HKUST-RockAI's Task 2 evaluation videos">Watch</a></td></tr>
            <tr class="is-prize"><td class="col-rank">3</td><th scope="row">Camelo</th><td>3rd place</td><td class="col-video"><a href="https://cloud.uni-hamburg.de/s/KbgEojL2QQTgA4R?dir=/Camelo" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Watch Camelo's Task 2 evaluation videos">Watch</a></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="col-rank">4</td><th scope="row">StarCore SJTU</th><td>—</td><td class="col-video">—</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="col-rank">5</td><th scope="row">EDL Team</th><td>—</td><td class="col-video">—</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="col-rank">5</td><th scope="row">ROBOT DREAMS</th><td>—</td><td class="col-video">—</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="col-rank">7</td><th scope="row">Sinica CITI Boy</th><td>—</td><td class="col-video">—</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="results-block results-table-wrap" id="task-3">
        <table>
          <caption><h2>Task 3 · Assisted Living &amp; Feeding</h2></caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Rank</th><th scope="col">Team</th><th scope="col">Award</th><th scope="col">Evaluation video</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="is-prize"><td class="col-rank">1</td><th scope="row">rl_alpha</th><td>1st place</td><td class="col-video"><a href="https://cloud.uni-hamburg.de/s/KbgEojL2QQTgA4R?dir=/rl_alpha" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Watch rl_alpha's Task 3 evaluation videos">Watch</a></td></tr>
            <tr class="is-prize"><td class="col-rank">2</td><th scope="row">Bierbyte</th><td>2nd place</td><td class="col-video"><a href="https://cloud.uni-hamburg.de/s/KbgEojL2QQTgA4R?dir=/Bierbyte" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Watch Bierbyte's Task 3 evaluation videos">Watch</a></td></tr>
            <tr class="is-prize"><td class="col-rank">3</td><th scope="row">EDL Team</th><td>3rd place</td><td class="col-video"><a href="https://cloud.uni-hamburg.de/s/KbgEojL2QQTgA4R?dir=/EDL%20Team_task3" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Watch EDL Team's Task 3 evaluation videos">Watch</a></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="col-rank">4</td><th scope="row">world model</th><td>—</td><td class="col-video">—</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="col-rank">5</td><th scope="row">AirSign</th><td>—</td><td class="col-video">—</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="results-block" id="prizes">
        <h2>Prizes</h2>
        <p>Places 1–3 in each task receive the Real-World Excellence prizes listed under <a href="competition.html#awards">Awards &amp; Prizes</a>. The cash component is awarded only to prize places with a score above zero. Prize places that scored zero receive the Franka Robotics purchase voucher, the trophy (1st place) and the special design gift, without cash. The organizers will email the winning teams about prize delivery. The Simulation Prize is not awarded in 2026. The InnoHub Special Award results will be announced separately.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="results-block" id="ranking-method">
        <h2>How teams were ranked</h2>
        <p>Few submissions scored above zero on real hardware. Teams with a score above zero are ranked by score. To rank the remaining teams, the organizing committee assessed how far each policy progressed during the official evaluations:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Task 2: grasp engagement first (whether the arm reached for the target and the gripper closed), then navigation.</li>
          <li>Task 3: navigation first (how far the robot navigated toward the table), then arm engagement.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Teams that could not be separated share a rank, and the next rank is skipped. The committee adopted this criterion after evaluation because the published criteria did not separate teams that scored zero. It applies only to those teams.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
{% endraw %}{% endblock %}
